  "topPRs": [
    {
      "id": "PR_kwDOJ_r-bs8AAAABFidrmg",
      "title": "ops: publish super-root dispute game impls in addresses.json",
      "author": "pauldowman",
      "number": 1353,
      "body": "As of Upgrade 20, chains register `SUPER_CANNON_KONA` (9) and `SUPER_PERMISSIONED` (5) in place of `CANNON` (0) and `PERMISSIONED_CANNON` (1). op-fetcher already reads both impls, but `config.Addresses` had no fields for them, so `CreateAddressesWithRolesFromFetcher` dropped them — and because `AddressesWithRoles.MarshalJSON` omits zero addresses, they disappeared silently.\n\nCodegen for a migrated chain therefore deletes `FaultDisputeGame` and `PermissionedDisputeGame` and publishes nothing in their place, which reads as unexplained data loss. That is likely why the daily codegen PRs have gone unmerged since #1339: twelve are now open, and the diff has grown from 12 deletions in #1347 to 34 deletions and 8 additions across 17 chains in #1352, holding up unrelated `MIPS`, `PreimageOracle` and `DelayedWETHProxy` updates.\n\n- Add `SuperFaultDisputeGame` and `SuperPermissionedDisputeGame` to `config.Addresses`, mapped from the fetcher output.\n- Cover the mapping with tests for the legacy-only and super-only cases.\n\nVerified on Sepolia: chains 11155420, 1301, 1946 and 763373 have `gameImpls(0)` and `gameImpls(1)` at zero, with only `gameImpls(5)` and `gameImpls(9)` set.\n\nDeliberately not addressed here:\n\n- `FaultDisputeGameCannonKonaImpl` is dropped by the same mapping. It degrades to a stale value rather than a missing key, and the naming convention does not extend cleanly, so it wants its own discussion.\n- `convertToScriptChainConfig` in `ops/internal/manage/codegen_test.go` zeroes every address, so no test asserts the contents of the generated addresses.json. That is the guard that would have caught this.\n- `op-core/superchain`'s `AddressesConfig` and kona's `AddressList` mirror this struct and need the same fields before downstream consumers can read the new keys.\n- The `Challenger` removal for these chains is correct and is not a regression: `SuperPermissionedDisputeGame` has no challenger role, and invalid proposals are handled by the Guardian via `AnchorStateRegistry.blacklistDisputeGame`.",
      "repository": "ethereum-optimism/superchain-registry",
      "createdAt": "2026-09-28T16:44:38Z",
      "mergedAt": "2026-09-28T21:46:17Z",
      "additions": 70,
      "deletions": 0
    },
